      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T18:19:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? Converting the value to a reference with as_ref() and then immediately dereferencing with \\* is unnecessary and potentially problematic in this case.\n\nThis can be dangerous as the temporary value is dropped at the end of the statement, potentially leaving a dangling reference. Rust\u0027s ownership and borrowing rules are designed to prevent this, and bypassing them with \\* can introduce memory safety issues.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1438,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 1438,
        "endChar": 97
      },
      "revId": "4c1d082b076ac1b0693e23bc0299e59feec06072",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a195a62_de27e286",
        "filename": "android/virtmgr/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
